==Sport Relief Does Strictly Come Dancing==

===2008===
A ''Strictly Come Dancing'' one-off special for [[Sport Relief]] was broadcast on 14 March 2008, with [[Craig Revel Horwood]], [[Arlene Phillips]] and [[Len Goodman]] judging. Five former ''Strictly'' contestants related to sport partnered a new celebrity.<ref>{{cite web| title = Strictly Sport Relief |  url = https://www.bbc.co.uk/programmes/b006m8dq| publisher=BBC | date=15 January 2008| access-date =18 January 2008 | url-status = live |archive-url = https://web.archive.org/web/20080119030110/http://www.bbc.co.uk/strictlycomedancing/news/2008/01/15/52036.shtml <!-- Bot retrieved archive --> |archive-date = 19 January 2008}}</ref> Jade Johnson and Kara Tointon were contestants on the main show in 2009 and 2010, with Johnson leaving after an injury, and Tointon winning the 2010 title. Their partners on their series were Ian Waite and Artem Chigvintsev.

